 "post": {
  "caption": "Plato's Gyges used a ring of invisibility to kill a king. But the real Gyges, in Herodotus, rose to power because he was seen. And in 1976, masked trick-or-treaters showed what anonymity does to us.\nWhat would you do first if nobody could see you?",
  "tags": [
   "#philosophy",
   "#plato",
   "#thoughtexperiment",
   "#ethics",
   "#psychology"
  ],
  "youtube_title": "Would You Stay Good If You Were Invisible?"
 }
}